<title>JAPAN: Japan March pork imports up 17.7 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March pork imports up 17.7 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in March totalled 23,233 tonnes, up 17.7 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Mar 97	Feb 97	 Mar 96</p>
<p> Total	     23,233	19,708	 19,741</p>
<p> Refrigerated     9,748	10,490	 10,992</p>
<p> Frozen	    13,485	 9,218	  8,749</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     3,280	 4,884	  1,219</p>
<p> U.S.		 5,525	 4,769	  5,723</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Mar 97	Feb 97	 Mar 96</p>
<p> Taiwan	    10,645	 3,907	 5,790</p>
<p>Total imports of refrigerated pork in the first three months of calendar 1997 totalled 29,630 tonnes, against 30,247 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Total imports of frozen pork in the January-March period of this year totalled 47,429 tonnes, against 36,290 tonnes a year earlier, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
